// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`what an agent is told about the knowledge Claude Code, auto mode 1`] = `
{
  "folder": {
    "--add-dir": "/data/knowledge/p1",
  },
  "prompt": 
"Run the tests

When you are done, call the \`report_step\` tool exactly once, as your last action. Use outcome "pass" when the task is done, "fail" when it is not, and "needs-input" when you need a person to decide or provide something. Put a one or two sentence summary of the result in \`summary\`. If you learned something about this project that would help the next agent, add it to \`learnings\`: a list of short notes. Leave it out otherwise.

To find something in the project knowledge, call \`search_knowledge\` with a few keywords or a question. It finds sections of files by their words, and by their meaning when this computer can. PDF and Word files too. Then read a file it gives with \`read_knowledge\`: give the hit's section, page or line to read from there."
,
  "system": "Project knowledge is in /data/knowledge/p1. Read INDEX.md there first, then grep the folder for what you need. Do not change the folder.",
  "tools": [
    "report_step",
    "search_knowledge",
    "read_knowledge",
  ],
}
`;

